{"authored" [{"question" "q-318975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $|\\,t\\,|=\\sqrt{2}$ and the angle between vectors $t$ and $u$ is $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ Find the scalar projection of $t$ onto $u.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{u}\\,t=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-318975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{u}\\,t & =|\\,t\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}cos\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-318975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "063df9d32c7b7bbea1e614df42642d34cda64b6b0566b4034b16eb743f7d8016" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-318975" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-318975" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $c=⟨4,-3,0⟩$ and $d=⟨2,1,-2⟩.$ Find, ${\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c-{\\text{comp}}_{c}\\,d.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c-{\\text{comp}}_{c}\\,d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{|\\,d\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{|\\,c\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{5} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c-{\\text{comp}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{5}{3}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "063df9d32c7b7bbea1e614df42642d34cda64b6b0566b4034b16eb743f7d8016" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275247" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-237016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ x \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-237016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot x+1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2-2x & =0 \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-237016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "063df9d32c7b7bbea1e614df42642d34cda64b6b0566b4034b16eb743f7d8016" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-237016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Cours