m" "value" "Let $p=⟨-1,1,2⟩$ and $q=⟨4,x,1⟩.$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is zero, find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "e178efe0503452c947df6835b908700d28bbbbe708604a9d6ea25edf5e2cbf29" "basis" 1085 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot x+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "e178efe0503452c947df6835b908700d28bbbbe708604a9d6ea25edf5e2cbf29" "basis" 1085 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8122f22a30d313865c55646d63ce92feeeacacacc47abc01b1aeb0480b235ffe" "basis" 1085 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "e178efe0503452c947df6835b908700d28bbbbe708604a9d6ea25edf5e2cbf29" "basis" 1085 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "e178efe0503452c947df6835b908700d28bbbbe708604a9d6ea25edf5e2cbf29" "basis" 1085 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "e178efe0503452c947df6835b908700d28bbbbe708604a9d6ea25edf5e2cbf29" "basis" 1085 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "e178efe0503452c947df6835b908700d28bbbbe708604a9d6ea25edf5e2cbf29" "basis" 1085 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "e178efe0503452c947df6835b908700d28bbbbe708604a9d6ea25edf5e2cbf29" "basis" 1085 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "e178efe0503452c947df6835b908700d28bbbbe708604a9d6ea25edf5e2cbf29" "basis" 1085 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-71527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $|\\,p\\,|=\\sqrt{3}$ and the angle between vectors $p$ and $q$ is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Find the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-71527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =|\\,p\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-71527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fcb7ef625b594b317187e59a3360275bf90c09e83972bf61a90c30f6b704e2d"} {"question" "q-71527" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-71527" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-71527" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-318975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $|\\,t\\,|=\\sqrt{2}$ and the angle between vectors $t$ and $u$ is $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ Find the scalar projection of $t$ onto $u.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{u}\\,t=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-318975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{u}\\,t & =|\\,t\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}cos\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-318975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fcb7ef625b594b317187e59a3360275bf90c09e83972bf61a90c30f6b704e2d"} {"question" "q-318975" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-318975" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-71532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $|\\,c\\,|=18$ and the angle between vectors $c$ and $d$ is $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ Find the scalar projection of $c$ onto $d.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-71532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =|\\,c\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =18\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =18\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-9\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-71532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fcb7ef625b594b317187e59a3360275bf90c09e83972bf61a90c30f6b704e2d"} {"question" "q-71532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-71532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-9"] ["math" "-9\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "9\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-71532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-9\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-126498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $|\\,c\\,|=5$ and the angle between vectors $c$ and $d$ is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Find the scalar projection of $c$ onto $d.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-126498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =|\\,c\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-126498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fcb7ef625b594b317187e59a3360275bf90c09e83972bf61a90c30f6b704e2d"} {"question" "q-126498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-126498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "-\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-126498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-318976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $|\\,r\\,|=3\\sqrt{3}$ and the angle between vectors $r$ and $s$ is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Find the scalar projection of $r$ onto $s.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{s}\\,r=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-318976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{s}\\,r & =|\\,r\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-318976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fcb7ef625b594b317187e59a3360275bf90c09e83972bf61a90c30f6b704e2d"} {"question" "q-318976" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-318976" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-101526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨3,-1,-1⟩$ and $b=⟨4,4,2⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-101526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-101526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fcb7ef625b594b317187e59a3360275bf90c09e83972bf61a90c30f6b704e2d"} {"question" "q-101526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-101526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-101526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨1,4,2\\sqrt{2}⟩$ and $q=⟨1,1,\\sqrt{2}⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p+{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1+2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,p\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p+{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{9}{5} \\\\  & =9(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =9(\\frac{5}{10}+\\frac{2}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fcb7ef625b594b317187e59a3360275bf90c09e83972bf61a90c30f6b704e2d"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{29}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{29}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{63}{10}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{63}{10}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-275247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $c=⟨4,-3,0⟩$ and $d=⟨2,1,-2⟩.$ Find, ${\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c-{\\text{comp}}_{c}\\,d.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c-{\\text{comp}}_{c}\\,d=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-275247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{|\\,d\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{|\\,c\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{5} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c-{\\text{comp}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{5}{3}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-275247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fcb7ef625b594b317187e59a3360275bf90c09e83972bf61a90c30f6b704e2d"} {"question" "q-275247" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-275247" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-101528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2,-1,2⟩$ and $b=⟨6,2,-3⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-101528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 6+(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-3)}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{|\\,a\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{4}{7}-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{7}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{3}{21}-\\frac{7}{21}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-101528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fcb7ef625b594b317187e59a3360275bf90c09e83972bf61a90c30f6b704e2d"} {"question" "q-101528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-101528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{16}{21}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{7}"] ["math" "-\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{4}{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-101528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{16}{21}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-19139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨3,2,1⟩$ and $b=⟨3,4,1⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-19139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{26}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-19139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fcb7ef625b594b317187e59a3360275bf90c09e83972bf61a90c30f6b704e2d"} {"question" "q-19139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-19139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}}"] ["math" "\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{14}}"] ["math" "\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{26}}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{14}}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{26}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-19139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{26}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-237017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=i-3j$ and $q=xi+2j+k.$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-237017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =1\\cdot x+(-3)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ x-6 & =0 \\\\ x & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dc2c79743d54bad34f4c6d186f97d2b9552bb5fb7ccee0f0c12278abbfd3e2b"} {"question" "q-237017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :questi