= 13 \\cdot  ( - \\frac{1}{2} ) \\\\  & = - \\frac{13}{2} .\\end{array}$$"] [17592186105412 :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,3,-1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,-7,0 \\rangle$. Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$."] [17592186105412 :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\text{comp}}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\, \\mathbf{a} & = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  \\mathbf{b}}{| \\, \\mathbf{b} \\, |} \\\\  & = \\frac{{a}_{x} {b}_{x} + {a}_{y} {b}_{y} + {a}_{z} {b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2} + {b}_{y}^{2} + {b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & = \\frac{3 \\cdot  2 + 3 \\cdot  ( - 7 ) + ( - 1 ) \\cdot  0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2} + ( - 7 {)}^{2} + {0}^{2}}} \\\\  & = - \\frac{15}{\\sqrt{53}} .\\end{array}$$"] [17592186105413 :question/problem "Let \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n and \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b}=\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 \\\\ - 4 \\\\ 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$."] [17592186105413 :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\text{comp}}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\, \\mathbf{a} & = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  \\mathbf{b}}{| \\, \\mathbf{b} \\, |} \\\\  & = \\frac{{a}_{x} {b}_{x} + {a}_{y} {b}_{y} + {c}_{z} {b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2} + {b}_{y}^{2} + {b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & = \\frac{0 \\cdot  2 + 0 \\cdot  ( - 4 ) + 1 \\cdot  0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2} + ( - 4 {)}^{2} + {0}^{2}}} \\\\  & = \\frac{0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2} + ( - 4 {)}^{2} + {0}^{2}}} \\\\  & = 0.\\end{array}$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186103037 17592186103038 17592186103039 17592186103040 17592186103041 17592186104952 17592186104953 17592186104954 17592186104955 17592186104956 17592186275264 17592186275265 17592186275266 17592186275267 17592186275268 17592186275288 17592186275289 17592186275302 17592186286188 17592186286189 17592186286190 17592186286191 17592186286192] "immu